 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Grammar · đã + verb (the past)",
     "texto": [
      "**đã** before the verb can show that an action has already happened: **Tôi đã đi làm** = I already went to work / I have gone to work.",
      "If the context already makes clear when it happened, it is often left out: **Hôm qua tôi đi làm** = yesterday I went to work. It is not a compulsory past tense form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "rồi (already)",
     "texto": [
      "**rồi** can mark that something has already happened or that a situation has already been reached. In simple sentences it usually comes at the end: **Tôi đi làm rồi** = I've already been to work.",
      "Its position depends on the sentence structure; to begin with, learn this common pattern. **đã** and **rồi** can appear together in some contexts, although you don't need to combine them in the examples in this lesson.",
      "**Rồi.** on its own also means «OK, understood», and it is used a lot to end a call."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "nữa (more, another)",
     "texto": [
      "With amounts, **nữa** means «more» or «another». It goes like this: amount + noun + **nữa**.",
      "**ba tháng nữa** = three more months (or «in three months») · **một ly nữa** = another glass."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
